        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fireworks custom deployment fallback with business hours and scaling",
        "summary": "Fireworks requests for `minimax/minimax-m2.5` now route to a custom deployment (`accounts/james-65d217/deployments/qne3jo8v`) during business hours (10am - 8pm ET) and fall back to the standard API (`accounts/fireworks/models/minimax-m2p5`) on `503 DEPLOYMENT_SCALING_UP`. `web/src/llm-api/fireworks.ts` adds `isDeploymentHours` for timezone checks and `DEPLOYMENT_COOLDOWN_MS` (2 minutes) to pause deployment attempts after scaling failures. `createFireworksRequest` accepts `modelIdOverride` to swap deployment IDs, while `parseFireworksErrorFromText` extracts status/text to allow non-scaling 503s to throw immediately. Scope limited to `web/src/llm-api/fireworks.ts` and `__tests__/fireworks-deployment.test.ts`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T01:43:52.092Z"
