        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add experimental /connect:chatgpt OAuth direct routing",
        "summary": "New CLI command `/connect:chatgpt` enables direct OpenAI subscription OAuth streaming, bypassing backend routing for eligible models. Feature gated by `CHATGPT_OAUTH_ENABLED=false` default; uses PKCE flow with local credential storage and refresh mutex. Scope covers CLI components, SDK provider logic, and shared constants; non-streaming requests remain backend-routed.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T01:42:20.890Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you opt in by enabling a special setting (it is off by default), you can now sign into ChatGPT directly from the command-line tool instead of going through the usual middleman service. When turned on, your subscription requests stream straight to OpenAI using a standard secure login flow, and your credentials are saved locally so you don't have to log in again. If you prefer the existing setup or your account isn't eligible for direct streaming, nothing changes, requests still route the old way unless you explicitly connect.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "31d358eaa2a9",
