        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Block non-US/CA IPs from free mode",
        "summary": "Free mode requests now fail with 403 free_mode_unavailable if the client IP resolves outside US or CA. Web API `web/src/app/api/v1/chat/completions/_post.ts` uses `geoip-lite` to check country codes, while CLI `cli/src/hooks/helpers/send-message.ts` surfaces the error via `isFreeModeUnavailableError`. Logic fails open if IP detection returns null, accommodating VPNs or proxies.",
        "significance": "major",
        "at": "2026-09-15T01:42:15.519Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use Codebuff for free from outside the United States or Canada, your chat session will now be blocked and you'll see a message telling you to upgrade to a paid plan. The service checks your internet address to guess your country, and if it doesn't recognize the address, say, because you're using a VPN, it lets you through. This filtering is enforced at the server level and surfaced through error handling in the CLI, so you'd notice it as an immediate stop to your run with a clear explanation rather than a silent failure.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "f3e3e1bc57cb",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:56:31.445Z"
